Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:27:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] log PipeWire versions and enforce the 1.4.2 runtime floor

PipeASIO 1.5 supports PipeWire 1.4.2 and newer. Enforce that same floor inside the driver for both the loaded client library and the connected daemon, so a post-install downgrade or manually sideloaded runtime cannot enter an unsupported compatibility path.

Reject an old loaded client before pw_init or any context setup. The daemon version arrives in pw_core_info during audio_open initial sync. A strict shared parser accepts normal package suffixes, rejects malformed or missing versions, and has native boundary coverage. An append-only audio status carries a focused Init failure across WoW64 without adding a new Unix call.

Keep logging daemon, client, and header versions. Keep the dynamic audio-node proxy tracking from the earlier design so node.force-quantum changes remain visible without node removal, but remove the pre-1.2 power-of-two envelope and its PE/WoW64 query.
